{"ts":"2026-08-10T06:07:39.802Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"507208966ab0dc1f88c5707f","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rl-swa0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The shared script launcher skipped every gate it guarded when a path could not be resolved"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"isMainInvocation caught a realpathSync failure and returned false, which makes runIfMain treat a direct invocation as a library import and skip main, so the docstring and coverage gates exit zero having done nothing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["coverage","gate","release"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-10T06:07:39.802Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T06:07:39.802Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a9e9b8ec8a166f037c53722236900f117999f38fd1470af27882d84e4bdbb809","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T06:08:02.837Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"507208966ab0dc1f88c5707f","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T06:08:02.837Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-10T06:08:02.837Z","author":"claude","text":"Three separate tests asserted the old behaviour, in docstring-gate, quality-scripts and coverage-gate. The coverage-gate one is the clearest statement of the cost: it expected false for an unresolvable entry, which is precisely the path where the coverage gate would exit zero having measured nothing."}]}],"before_hash":"a9e9b8ec8a166f037c53722236900f117999f38fd1470af27882d84e4bdbb809","after_hash":"416e4755349eda2e15771fa2f19f7a006bd79dcc638eecfe77e737e6657cd6c8"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T06:08:03.263Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"507208966ab0dc1f88c5707f","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T06:08:03.263Z","author":"claude","text":"This repository and pm-linear both hid the defect behind a shared script-launcher.ts that the gate only re-exports, which is why a fleet survey of scripts/docstring-gate.ts reported them clean. Factoring a defect out of the file people search makes it invisible to the search."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T06:08:03.263Z"}],"before_hash":"416e4755349eda2e15771fa2f19f7a006bd79dcc638eecfe77e737e6657cd6c8","after_hash":"22aecc1a6dd067d5d2c3b61846a99056d193a5642d80b4395d7ef2acfe32991b"}
